Subject: [PATCH] feat(billing): /billing/offer carries the plan prices
 (frontend 05:10Z, Misho)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The frontend's 05:10Z: Misho decided the app reads the plan prices from
the server instead of carrying them. The pricing page and the earnings
page („spend on a month") hold $19.99 / $79.00 as constants today.

GET /billing/offer gains plans: { pro, enterprise }, USD a month. The
prices come from provider_prices subscription.price.* (migration 035), the
same rows a month bought with the referral balance is charged from, so the
page and that charge cannot disagree. A tier with no row, or a price of
0, is null, and the page keeps its own value. Live today the rows hold
19.99 and 79.00, so nothing a person sees changes.

FOR_FRONTEND has the contract. A card subscription is charged at the
payment provider's own price; that is noted there and for ops.

DONE WHEN: the route answers plans { pro: 19.99, enterprise: 79 } on live,
and both pages show the server's numbers.

